  "historyText": "Arcade Video game published 42 years ago:\n\nHyper Sports (c) 1984 Konami\n\nExport release. Game developed in Japan. See the original for more information; \"Hyper Olympic '84 [Model GX330]\".\n\n- TECHNICAL -\n\nGame ID: GX330\n\n- TRIVIA -\n\nHyper Sports was released in July 1984 by Centuri in the US, under license from Konami. \n\nKelly Kobashigawa holds the official record for this game with 538340 points.\n\n- PORTS -\n\n* COMPUTERS: \n[EU] BBC Micro (1984) \n[EU] MSX (1984) \"Hyper Sports 1 [Model RC715]\" \n[EU] MSX (1984) \"Hyper Sports 2 [Model RC717]\" \n[EU] MSX (1985) \"Hyper Sports 3 [Model RC733]\" \n[EU] Commodore 64 (1984) \"Hyper Sports [Model 120060]\"\n[EU] Commodore 16 (1986) \"3 Konami Coin-Op Hits [Model 110122]\"\n[EU] Sinclair ZX Spectrum (1985) \n[EU] Amstrad CPC (1986)\n\n- SERIES -\n\n1. Track & Field [Model GX361] (1983, ARC)\n2. Hyper Sports [Model GX330] (1984, ARC)\n3. '88 Games [Model GX861] (1988, ARC)\n4. Hyper Athlete [Model GV021] (1996, ARC)\n5. Nagano Winter Olympics '98 [Model GX720] (1998, ARC)\n6. International Track & Field 2000 (2000, PS)\n7. International Track & Field Summer Games (2000, N64)\n8. New International Track & Field (2008, DS)\n9. Hyper Sports Winter (2010 iPhone)\n10. Hyper Sports Track & Field (2010 iPhone)\n\n- CONTRIBUTE -\n\nEdit this entry: https://www.arcade-history.com/game/1164/?o=2",
  "historyCredit": "Story courtesy of Gaming History (arcade-history.com)"
